  "subject": "a volunteer on the January black-faced spoonbill census at a Tainan fish-pond roost at half past five, counting sleeping birds through a scope in the north wind while a retired teacher clicks the tally counter, losing the count at 240 when a kite circles and the whole flock lifts, and starting again to find twenty more than last year",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien math rock in the melodic, bass-led Taiwanese style. Two clean electric guitars playing interlocking two-hand tapped arpeggios in 7/8 that snap into 4/4 on the choruses; a melodic electric bass carrying its own countermelody high on the neck; busy, crisp live drums with ghost notes and sudden stops; a glockenspiel doubling the counting phrases. Dry, bright, close studio mix with air between the parts. A soft, clear female alto, plain and conversational, with a lower harmony doubling the counting lines. 136 BPM, E major. Cold-fingered, patient and quietly delighted. No distorted power chords, no screamed vocals, no autotune, no synth pads, no post-rock crescendo, no indie-pop strummed chords.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n一月透早 五點半\n北風 對魚塭頂吹過來\n千里鏡 架佇岸頂\n我的指頭仔 冷甲袂振動\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n退休的林老師 提一个計數器\n伊講 你算 我按\n\n[Chorus]\n一 二 三 四 五\n一隻一隻 白甲若雪\n喙 攏藏佇翼股底\n算到一半 閣徙位\n\n[Verse]\n天光矣 才看會清\n烏烏的面 若像毋捌洗\n喙 若一支飯匙\n佇水底 左掃右掃\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n林老師細聲講 喘氣莫傷大聲\n計數器 按到兩百三\n\n[Chorus]\n一 二 三 四 五\n兩百三十一 三十二\n一隻掃一下 閣睏落去\n林老師 對我笑一下\n\n[Verse]\n一隻鶆鴞 佇天頂踅一輾\n規片白的 一下攏飛起來\n若像一領被 予人掀開\n計數器 停佇兩百四\n\n[Bridge]\n落來矣 一隻 閣一隻\n林老師 共計數器歸零\n伊講 無要緊 咱重算\n\n[Chorus]\n一 二 三 四 五\n一隻一隻 白甲若雪\n三百一十二 算予清楚\n比舊年 加二十隻\n\n[Outro]\n明年一月 閣來算",
